# Blue Pencil: house overlay (example)

Copy this file to `local.md` in the same folder and edit it. Blue Pencil reads `local.md` before
anything else, and its rules override SKILL.md where they differ. Keep it out of version
control: it usually holds private paths and tool names.

## Language

- Report language: English, whatever language the user writes in.
- House writing rules: follow `~/notes/style-guide.md` in every rewrite.

## Paths

- Reports: `~/work/copy-reviews/<domain>-<YYYY-MM-DD>/` instead of `./bluepencil-reports/`.
- Crawls: `~/work/crawls/<domain>.md`.
- Our client sites live in `~/work/clients/<domain>/`. Read the repo as well as the crawl.

## Tools

- Mobile screenshot: `npx playwright screenshot --viewport-size=390,844 <url> <report>/shots/390.png`
- Search Console: `gsc-export --site sc-domain:<domain> --page <url> --days 90 > <report>/gsc.csv`
- Analytics: GA4 property per site is listed in `~/work/clients/<domain>/analytics.txt`.

## Conventions

- Product docs in our repos are called `BRIEF.md`, not `PRODUCT.md`.
- Price data lives in `src/data/prices.json`. Check every price claim against it.
- Before review, check that the brief describes this site and not a sister site.
- Never name a competitor in a client report. Write "a competitor in the same town".
